# Backend Gap Analysis: Workflow Support

**Date:** 2025-01-30  
**Status:** Analysis Complete  
**Purpose:** Map 9-phase workflow system + 15 application types to current backend capabilities

---

## Executive Summary

**Critical Finding:** The current backend (14 crates, 37 MCP tools) provides **foundational infrastructure** (auth, audit, commands, snapshots) but lacks **workflow orchestration** and **project lifecycle management** capabilities.

**Gap Severity:**
- 🔴 **Blocking:** 6 missing core systems (no workaround)
- 🟡 **High Impact:** 8 missing modules (workflow degraded)
- 🟢 **Enhancement:** 4 missing features (nice-to-have)

**Estimated Scope:**
- New Crates: **6-9**
- Database Migrations: **8-12**
- New MCP Tools: **35-45**
- Service Layer Functions: **50-70**

---

## Part 1: Current Backend Inventory

### Existing Crates (14)

| Crate | Purpose | Workflow Support |
|-------|---------|------------------|
| `authority-domain` | Domain types (ActorScope, BoundedCommand, SkillGrant) | ✅ Actor/skill model |
| `policy-engine` | Policy evaluation (authorize_action) | ✅ Permission checks |
| `audit-log` | Audit event types, hashing | ✅ Change tracking |
| `snapshot-ledger` | Snapshot manifests, content addressing | ✅ Version control |
| `control-store` | PostgreSQL persistence (CoreStore) | ✅ Data layer |
| `control-service` | Service layer (business logic) | ⚠️ Partial orchestration |
| `control-api` | REST API (Axum) | ✅ HTTP interface |
| `operator-cli` | CLI tool | ✅ Admin operations |
| `agent-mcp` | MCP protocol (tool definitions + handler) | ✅ Agent interface |
| `object-store` | S3-compatible object storage | ✅ Artifact storage |
| `rollback-engine` | Rollback preview/execution | ✅ Undo operations |
| `gateway` | Gateway logic | ✅ Entry point |
| `knowledge-store` | Knowledge metadata | ⚠️ Limited to knowledge |
| `bundle-runtime` | Bundle deployment/runtime | ✅ Deployment |

**Strengths:**
- Rock-solid permission/audit/command foundation
- Event sourcing + snapshot + rollback architecture
- MCP tooling for agent interaction
- Object storage for artifacts

**Weaknesses:**
- No project/workflow entity
- No phase state machine
- No gate enforcement system
- No artifact repository (beyond object-store primitives)
- No team/skill assignment tracking

### Existing MCP Tools (37)

**Well-Covered Domains:**
- ✅ Session management (issue, renew, revoke)
- ✅ Command lifecycle (propose, authorize, apply)
- ✅ Audit chain (query, verify)
- ✅ Snapshots (create, validate, compare)
- ✅ Rollbacks (preview, execute, verify)
- ✅ Actor/skills (get scope, register, activate)
- ✅ Gateway execution
- ✅ Bundle deployment
- ✅ Runtime management
- ✅ Live watch (monitoring, remediation)

**Under-Covered Domains:**
- ⚠️ Work packets (generated, but not tied to projects/phases)
- ⚠️ Knowledge (basic query/ingest, no structured artifact storage)
- ⚠️ Build watch (cost tracking, but no budget/approval workflow)

**Missing Domains:**
- ❌ Project/workflow management
- ❌ Gate approvals
- ❌ Artifact repository (requirements, designs, ADRs, test plans)
- ❌ Team assignment
- ❌ Application type registry
- ❌ Template library
- ❌ Security review tracking
- ❌ Test plan management
- ❌ Release orchestration

